{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming","id":801714,"title":"Okay, 20th Anniversary editions for the original five... any more coming?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-05T18:30:39-08:00","id":801714,"title":"Okay, 20th Anniversary editions for the original five... any more coming?","content":"I have to ask that. Is it under consideration? Is it something even possible now, with the new White Wolf ownership?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7242-velvet-elvis","name":"Velvet Elvis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T18:33:55-08:00","id":801715,"title":"","content":"White Wolf gave them the okay for Changeling20, so I don't see why not.<br /> <br /> I'm not looking forward to the wait for Demon20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T18:43:09-08:00","id":801721,"title":"","content":"Sure hope so. I'd love to see Hunter the Reckoning 20, Demon 20, and Kindred of the East 20. Would like see them all updated a bit before release, maybe a few changes(but not too many changes), and I'd be in for a deluxe edition on all three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T18:53:45-08:00","id":801724,"title":"","content":"Well, Hunter would be 2019, and Demon would be 2022 if we're planning on 20th anniversary editions...<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T20:54:47-08:00","id":801755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=801721#post801721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure hope so. I'd love to see Hunter the Reckoning 20, Demon 20, and Kindred of the East 20. Would like see them all updated a bit before release, maybe a few changes(but not too many changes), and I'd be in for a deluxe edition on all three.</div> </div> </div> </div>I distinctly remember one of the devs saying they wouldn't do KotE20. They said we'd sooner see a Vampire sourcebook about Asia than a revival of the Kuei-Jin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T21:40:45-08:00","id":801781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=801724#post801724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Hunter would be 2019, and Demon would be 2022 if we're planning on 20th anniversary editions...<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>And Mummy would be 2021, I think? I forget whether Year of the Scarab was immediately after Year of the Reckoning, or if there was another year between them. <br /> <br /> Also Mage would be 2013, Wraith would be 2014, and Changeling would be 2015; but at best, that's going to be 2015, 2016, and 2016 \u2014 and I'm not going to hold my breath waiting for that to happen. 2016\u20132017, and 2017\u20132018 strike me as more likely release Windows for Wraith and Changeling. Given that there appears to be a 1\u20132 year delay between KS launch and PDF release on the X20 lines, 2017\u20132018 would be a good timeframe for the H20 KS. And that's not <i>too</i> far away, all things considered. <br /> <br /> Or, you know, they could just switch to \u201cCommemorative Editions\u201d, and not worry if it falls on the 20th Anniversary of the original edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T21:40:46-08:00","id":801782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=801755#post801755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I distinctly remember one of the devs saying they wouldn't do KotE20. They said we'd sooner see a Vampire sourcebook about Asia than a revival of the Kuei-Jin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool. I know you don't want it. <br /> <br /> &quot;One of the devs&quot; doesn't speak for all of Onyx Path and/or White Wolf Publishing. He also wasn't a developer for KotE, so I'm not sure by what you mean by &quot;one of the devs.&quot; Regardless, that was his opinion as a freelancer, and frankly, it's one I don't happen to share. I know many people that would love to see a Kindred of the East Anniversary Edition, with a few changes and updates.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-06-2016, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T22:41:07-08:00","id":801809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=801755#post801755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I distinctly remember one of the devs saying they wouldn't do KotE20. They said we'd sooner see a Vampire sourcebook about Asia than a revival of the Kuei-Jin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And I remember Holden saying he'd love to Redo KOTE bring it more in line with Exalted!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T22:42:21-08:00","id":801810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=801781#post801781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Mummy would be 2021, I think? I forget whether Year of the Scarab was immediately after Year of the Reckoning, or if there was another year between them.<br /> <br /> Also Mage would be 2013, Wraith would be 2014, and Changeling would be 2015; but at best, that's going to be 2015, 2016, and 2016 \u2014 and I'm not going to hold my breath waiting for that to happen. 2016\u20132017, and 2017\u20132018 strike me as more likely release Windows for Wraith and Changeling. Given that there appears to be a 1\u20132 year delay between KS launch and PDF release on the X20 lines, 2017\u20132018 would be a good timeframe for the H20 KS. And that's not <i>too</i> far away, all things considered.<br /> <br /> Or, you know, they could just switch to \u201cCommemorative Editions\u201d, and not worry if it falls on the 20th Anniversary of the original edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rich mentioned in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/we-like-being-asked-anything-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">a previous Monday Meeting</a> that they'd have to do &quot;Anniversary Editions&quot; rather than &quot;20th Anniversary Editions&quot; for a couple of them, although he didn't mention which.<br /> <br /> Year-wise, it went Year of the Reckoning in 1999, Year of Revelations in 2000, and Year of the Scarab in 2001.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T03:11:37-08:00","id":801904,"title":"","content":"So, besides the chorus of, basically, we don't know if any of the post-original five lines are getting something...<br /> <br /> 1) I wouldn't mind seeing something more like &quot;WOD20&quot; esp. since KotE and MtC weren't even full corebooks, DtF reused a ton of VtM material, and so on. Though it would get a bit crowded... I might revise my dislike of a H20 that has HtR and the so-far-not-updated non-Imbued hunters into one big YotH book. Two books rather than four would mean we get them faster and all that.<br /> <br /> 2) David Hill is the developer that doesn't want to see KotE20. We had a big thread about it a while ago. And while he doesn't speak for Onyx Path or White Wolf, he <i>lives in Japan</i>. Given that he's one of the few people that might make the book that can attest to how the original books were received in an Asian country by actually asking people there, he's got a lot of sway on the subject. Given that he's related that KotE has a reputation with Japanese gamers similar to WOD: Gypsies has with Western gamers, I think Onyx Path and/or White Wolf would be hard pressed to simply ignore his feelings on whether or not KotE can be salvaged into something not horrible offensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T06:19:43-08:00","id":802049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=801904#post801904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) David Hill is the developer that doesn't want to see KotE20. We had a big thread about it a while ago. And while he doesn't speak for Onyx Path or White Wolf, he <i>lives in Japan</i>. Given that he's one of the few people that might make the book that can attest to how the original books were received in an Asian country by actually asking people there, he's got a lot of sway on the subject. Given that he's related that KotE has a reputation with Japanese gamers similar to WOD: Gypsies has with Western gamers, I think Onyx Path and/or White Wolf would be hard pressed to simply ignore his feelings on whether or not KotE can be salvaged into something not horrible offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'll disagree. David Hill is known for having some extremely strong political and social views that may or may not be in tune with gamers around the world. Going on one person's views simply because of they now live in Japan is not something I would do. KotE can and should be &quot;cleaned up&quot; by a collective group of people, gamers who, <b>regardless of their location</b>, deal with the subject matter in a respectful way.<br /> <br /> There's a VERY GOOD game beneath all of the messy stuff that can be found in Kindred of the East. I'm positive that a respectful, and intelligent group of developers could attack the project in a way that brings KotE to gamers in the modern era.<br /> <br /> These are my views, and you're welcome to disagree. I just feel it's foolish to take one person's opinion on something(who stated they didn't want to work on it in the first place), where it's clear there are MANY gamers in the world that loved Kindred of the East, and that there is a good game underneath it all.<br /> <br /> He doesn't want to work on it? Cool. I'm sure there are people that do. I'm not of the opinion that you have to live in the country in order to work on a project that contains it. Far more research is at our fingertips now than was in the 1990's. Far more.<br /> <br /> The city books and resources being produced now are better than anything we've gotten in the last 20 years. The internet is a wonderful thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-06-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T06:22:31-08:00","id":802050,"title":"","content":"This is the last I'll speak on it, too. Every time this subject comes up, it's always the same posters saying the same things about the same topic(myself, included).<br /> <br /> You don't want something? Don't buy it. Don't support it. But there are people that do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T09:18:40-08:00","id":802156,"title":"","content":"There are certain people that are <i>really into</i> (mostly Japanese/)Asian culture and feel that Western developers - for video games or any other thing - just can't &quot;do it right.&quot; Whether it's respecting a culture through primary source material or even capturing a specific cultural tone, there is a segment of people that feel only persons belonging to a specific culture should speak about said culture - whether it's fact or fiction, from film to role playing books. There are also people that feel any &quot;real world&quot; cultures absolutely should not be featured in a &quot;game,&quot; but that heads into a different discussion.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not a big fan of KotE, but that doesn't mean I'm going to demand it never be brought up again. In fact, I think an anniversary edition that cleans it up would be great, even if not for me. I know people like to poke fun at Ubisoft, but their &quot;A multicultural team...&quot; message at the beginning of their games is exactly what KotE could use - let's see if we can't &quot;fix&quot; it rather than bury it.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T17:45:41-08:00","id":802492,"title":"","content":"Going to add my voice to those who would want to see an Anniversary edition of Kindred of the East. David Hill is allowed to have his opinion but I am going to respectfully disagree. Materials in much more recently released by Onyx Path, both in Chronicles of Darkness and the World of Darkness have set some level of precedent for culturally rich gaming material and I don't think that KotE is somehow mysteriously except for those possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T18:49:36-08:00","id":802534,"title":"","content":"I believe the issue is that KotE would need to be rebuilt from the ground up to attain that level of quality - and at that point, is it really an anniversary edition? Let's remember that these anniversary editions - well, until Mage anyway - are not reboots and rebuilds so much as spit-shines on the existing product, setting, and ruleset to shine 'em up and make 'em sing again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T18:50:38-08:00","id":802536,"title":"","content":"Just gonna put out there that back in '06, the party line was still &quot;we will never publish new classic World of Darkness material&quot;, five years before V20 was released. Since then, I have refused to believe any statements of &quot;we will never publish new XX&quot;. I'm not a fan of KotE, but facts is facts: they say it's not happening up until it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T20:08:52-08:00","id":802614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802534#post802534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the issue is that KotE would need to be rebuilt from the ground up to attain that level of quality - and at that point, is it really an anniversary edition? Let's remember that these anniversary editions - well, until Mage anyway - are not reboots and rebuilds so much as spit-shines on the existing product, setting, and ruleset to shine 'em up and make 'em sing again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and considering that most of those changes, in language and the like, will be for a morally sound reason. Yeah I got no problem calling that an Anniversary edition. The differences wouldn't be so vast it would be like comparing WoD to ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T20:24:06-08:00","id":802620,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Kindred of the East be a supplemental part of the V20 line, like Vampire: Dark Ages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T20:34:51-08:00","id":802624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802620#post802620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Kindred of the East be a supplemental part of the V20 line, like Vampire: Dark Ages?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also a Wraith supplement, and it was based heavily on the Anime that was being fed to the US at the time. (And someone was a Hentai fan...)<br /> <br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T23:22:27-08:00","id":802804,"title":"","content":"the Hsien are going to be in C20 and... they were much less well recieved by any group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T00:37:12-08:00","id":802900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802620#post802620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Kindred of the East be a supplemental part of the V20 line, like Vampire: Dark Ages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, but they were pretty different mechanically from Cainites (and, well, different in nearly every way of course). They had more in common with Wraiths/Risen than Kindred, but were pretty cross-over unfriendly. They were more of a mini gameline than a VtM supplement.<br /> <br /> Which was why I didn't care for them. They were advertised as the &quot;Eastern Kindred&quot;, but couldn't really work with Kindred. Not mechanically, not thematically... Hell, they were explicitly stated to be antagonistic towards Western Kindred, so they literally couldn't work with Cainites. It almost felt like false advertising to call them the Kindred of the far East.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T00:52:12-08:00","id":802916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802900#post802900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of, but they were pretty different mechanically from Cainites (and, well, different in nearly every way of course). They had more in common with Wraiths/Risen than Kindred, but were pretty cross-over unfriendly. They were more of a mini gameline than a VtM supplement.<br /> <br /> Which was why I didn't care for them. They were advertised as the &quot;Eastern Kindred&quot;, but couldn't really work with Kindred. Not mechanically, not thematically... Hell, they were explicitly stated to be antagonistic towards Western Kindred, so they literally couldn't work with Cainites. It almost felt like false advertising to call them the Kindred of the far East.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> WHile I agree kOTE was a mechanical mess I would disagree that they thematically couldn't work with Kindred. I've had plenty of crossover games that didn't explode and had both sides differences support thematic growth in unique ways, it was in fact much easier to say get the contrasts of dharma and humanity vs the suppposed easily useable Paths since nearly every path user was in a &quot;can't interact with humanity types without violence or serious game bending&quot;<br /> <br /> Come to think of ot I'd argue KOTE was basically the Beast of CWOD it was the most crossover friendly, the only thing it really had issues with is Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T01:14:26-08:00","id":802923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802624#post802624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was also a Wraith supplement, and it was based heavily on the Anime that was being fed to the US at the time. (<u>And someone was a Hentai fan...)</u><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But enough about Obetenebration...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T01:54:07-08:00","id":802937,"title":"","content":"I think KotE is actually more offensive and problematic for Asian Americans than it is for the Japanese. The Japanese are a cultural and ethnic majority in Japan, so KotE doesn't really contribute to the daily oppression of Japanese people in Japan. It's laughable xenophobia and exoticism to them, much the same as the way we Brits laugh or roll our eyes at all the villains with Hollywood British accents in American films (or, vice versa, our own stereotypes of America). Likewise, I'm sure the French aren't particularly upset by British stereotypes of them in popular culture.<br /> <br /> However, Asians in America, who are a minority, are the ones who experience ridicule, racism and oppression because of the continued use of stereotypes about Asians in popular culture.<br /> <br /> So, arguably, the best people to write KotE wouldn't be people living in Asia but Asians living in America and the Diasporas (British Asians, French Asians, etc). It's they who'll benefit/suffer the most from how it turns out.<br /> <br /> I'm also aware this is largely a discussion being had by non-Asians. The discussion is likely to be biased or one-sided as a result. We might be missing the point entirely.<br /> <br /> Now, I would like to see a KotE20 done right. But I want it to be led by Asians. That's the only way to ensure the primary vision for the game isn't that of people who aren't impacted by the negative side effects of doing it wrong. It would also be nice if OPP were to make money from Asian culture that Asians actually get to make some money from it too, by hiring those writers.<br /> <br /> But I'm aware that probably won't happen (most of OPP's writers are white American dudes, which means investing in ways to address that and reaching out to writers who may just be offended by the whole thing), and I don't expect OPP particularly *wants* to engage with KotE any more anyway. OPP is as aware of the problems with the line as anyone, and from the work of Satyr on Mage, you can see there's a definite consciousness around the problems of representation within the gamelines.<br /> <br /> I think it's likely to remain a nostalgia thing. Although I wouldn't be surprised if there was a one-off rules update to streamline everything without having to do a whole core book. Such a thing might be better as a fan supplement anyway, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T02:55:49-08:00","id":802949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802916#post802916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHile I agree kOTE was a mechanical mess I would disagree that they thematically couldn't work with Kindred. I've had plenty of crossover games that didn't explode and had both sides differences support thematic growth in unique ways, it was in fact much easier to say get the contrasts of dharma and humanity vs the suppposed easily useable Paths since nearly every path user was in a &quot;can't interact with humanity types without violence or serious game bending&quot;<br /> <br /> Come to think of ot I'd argue KOTE was basically the Beast of CWOD it was the most crossover friendly, the only thing it really had issues with is Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I always ran into trouble when I'd try to integrate KotE in my games. They tended to come across as &quot;better than you&quot; kindred, since they were either as restricted on feeding or less restricted, with access to special magic rituals that didn't need a heavy XP investment, fewer weaknesses than Kindred, and if you were... Whichever it was, yin or yang balanced, you got to play in the sunlight. Really, the only thing that Kindred could do that Kuei-Jin couldn't is make minions; embracing and ghouling. And since they don't want Cainites on their turf and rarely leave their own turf, they only end up interacting with each other as antagonists.<br /> <br /> In fairness, I never tried using them in non-VtM games and I didn't get much use from them compared to other splats, so it could just be me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T04:39:41-08:00","id":802971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802949#post802949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness, I never tried using them in non-VtM games and I didn't get much use from them compared to other splats, so it could just be me.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really worked best on their own. Which was kinda the design idea behind them. I liked a lot of what of what did with them, and while some of the Orientalisam was downright offensive and done with some utterly bad research, as a whole it was a pretty cool idea for a game. And they cannot really walk in daylight for a long period of time, even when they are Yang imbalanced. Interestingly, they interact the best with the other Lotus games and Wraith as both Hengeyokai and Hsien key off certain political cues that allow interaction that is not necessarily hostile. Wraiths and interactions with the Umbra are key to actually playing KotE, and it helps if you got into it with some Werewolf and/or Wraith under the belt.<br /> <br /> The Dharmas were an especially intriguing prospect, and their guidebooks were pretty damn good, with Devil Tigers literally being mind blowing at the time. If anyone told me before that that the book would convince me that seeking to Ascend through becoming a perfect demon was a valid idea, I'd have laughed it off.<br /> <br /> I doubt we'd see a new version of it as is, but we are getting a lot of new stuff with Wraith 20 and Changeling 20, so it might come to be that we get another version of KotE. I would love if they kept the difference between them and vampires, as the themes and ideas offer a lot of good inspiration for games. I have never particularly liked Vampire, but Kindred of the East always had seeds of greatness within it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T07:49:13-08:00","id":803082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802900#post802900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of, but they were pretty different mechanically from Cainites (and, well, different in nearly every way of course). They had more in common with Wraiths/Risen than Kindred, but were pretty cross-over unfriendly. They were more of a mini gameline than a VtM supplement.<br /> <br /> Which was why I didn't care for them. They were advertised as the &quot;Eastern Kindred&quot;, but couldn't really work with Kindred. Not mechanically, not thematically... Hell, they were explicitly stated to be antagonistic towards Western Kindred, so they literally couldn't work with Cainites. It almost felt like false advertising to call them the Kindred of the far East.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's wasn't anything terribly concrete about the Asian undead in earlier works. With the Vancouver book detailing some of the Japanese groups through the lens of Kindred interpretation. That said when KotE was advertised it was painfully obvious that &quot;Kindred of the East&quot; was a stylization and that they were not literally Asian Cainites. Also yeah they can work with Kindred and there is even an entire sub group of them whose social and court status all revolves around being the face to Kindred interactions. The problem wasn't they(and they actually really just means your mandarins and the like) couldn't work with the Kindred. It was how much of the early materials focused on &quot;Kill whitey.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T07:53:00-08:00","id":803087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802949#post802949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I always ran into trouble when I'd try to integrate KotE in my games. They tended to come across as &quot;better than you&quot; kindred, since they were either as restricted on feeding or less restricted</div> </div> </div> </div>About as restricted. Kindred can feed on anything with blood; Wan Gui could only feed on humans and other monsters. Even their use of feeding on ambient energy wouldn't grant that much of it, unless they ripped it out, which as far as I can gather would have political consequences in angering their non-vampire associates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with access to special magic rituals that didn't need a heavy XP investment </div> </div> </div>The powerful ones typically required Rituals at six or seven dots or more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> fewer weaknesses than Kindred </div> </div> </div>Nearly double cost to raise Disciplines compared to Kindred Clan Disciplines, with no cost breaks, ever. Their main sources for soaking aggravated damage, to the extent any vampires did, also sucked. Finally, their multiple action powers were nothing compared to Celerity when they were introduced in 2nd edition. But then, Celerity was always kind of stupidly overpowered until DA Vampire and V20. Then it just became as overpowered as any other extra actions power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and if you were... Whichever it was, yin or yang balanced, you got to play in the sunlight. </div> </div> </div>Yang Imbalanced vampires could stay out in direct sunlight for maybe up to slightly less than a half an hour, which was counterbalanced with getting hungrier far more often and being extra flammable and capable of catching diseases. Meanwhile, the Yin Imbalanced suffered extra hard. Both states required some incredibly lopsided Virtue allotments (one three dots higher than the other), and would seriously dig at the other if you had it, which is important, because it meant having a very low equivalent to Courage or Self-Control, the latter case compounding the early feelings of being ravenous and uncontrollably hungry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, the only thing that Kindred could do that Kuei-Jin couldn't is make minions; embracing and ghouling. And since they don't want Cainites on their turf and rarely leave their own turf, they only end up interacting with each other as antagonists. </div> </div> </div>You're leaving out the blood bond. That's fairly important; a similar capacity requires Obligation 5 for Demon People, which is a higher xp investment than an in-clan Discipline at six dots (90 xp vs 85). Combined with ghouls, that can be a rather pronounced power difference over time, compared to the capacity to make dhampyr that take way longer to develop into power and are affected by age, albeit loosely enough that the note on three-hundred year old dhampyrs was perplexing (aging at slightly less than one year per decade, said dhampyr would be about like a late middle-aged persona, at worst). Also, you have to be Yang imbalanced to produce dhampyrs, and getting them involved is often frowned upon by the behavior that keeps your power stat up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-07-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T08:28:19-08:00","id":803109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802923#post802923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But enough about Obetenebration...</div> </div> </div> </div> Or Freak Legion. Or a few other places.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T09:57:32-08:00","id":803175,"title":"","content":"Gah! Alright, I guess I never really gave KotE a fair shake. Carry on!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T10:55:33-08:00","id":803214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802620#post802620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Kindred of the East be a supplemental part of the V20 line, like Vampire: Dark Ages?</div> </div> </div> </div>A curious comparison \u2013 when coupled with the invocation of David A. Hill's name, the Developer of <b>V20: Dark Ages</b> \u2013 that said book has the MOST references to the vampires of <b>Kindred of the East</b> in any of the World of Darkness 20 books... Yes, the references are all to the Wan Kuei of the Fourth Age, and it's all in association with Salubri of the Wu Zao caste. However, it's there, and what's there is reasonably consistent with <b>Kindred of the East</b> or at the very least the <i>Blood and Silk</i> supplement.<br /> <br /> The above neither proves nor disproves anything, but it's worth mention. Oh, I think that the Kuei-Jin are named in another <b>V20</b> book, but I can't remember which one. Maybe <i>Anarchs Unbound</i>? Again, not proof, but more fuel for the fire if nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:49:00-08:00","id":803336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=802949#post802949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I always ran into trouble when I'd try to integrate KotE in my games. They tended to come across as &quot;better than you&quot; kindred, since they were either as restricted on feeding or less restricted, with access to special magic rituals that didn't need a heavy XP investment, fewer weaknesses than Kindred, and if you were... Whichever it was, yin or yang balanced, you got to play in the sunlight. Really, the only thing that Kindred could do that Kuei-Jin couldn't is make minions; embracing and ghouling. And since they don't want Cainites on their turf and rarely leave their own turf, they only end up interacting with each other as antagonists.<br /> <br /> In fairness, I never tried using them in non-VtM games and I didn't get much use from them compared to other splats, so it could just be me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> KOTE rituals are no easier ot get for the average KJ than Blood magic rituals are for Blood mages. If you can handle a Tremere, or far worse a Giovanni KOTE rituals are childs play. A number of Kindred Disciplines had no parallel among the KJ and vice versa. As for slightly different weaknesses, I am damn sure if they were just clan weaknesses no one would balk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T19:03:19-08:00","id":803495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803336#post803336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KOTE rituals are no easier ot get for the average KJ than Blood magic rituals are for Blood mages. If you can handle a Tremere, or far worse a Giovanni KOTE rituals are childs play. A number of Kindred Disciplines had no parallel among the KJ and vice versa. As for slightly different weaknesses, I am damn sure if they were just clan weaknesses no one would balk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bone Flowers introduced a theoretical equivalence for some necromancy rituals, requiring Rituals at one level higher than the minimum Discipline rating of the ritual to be learned, and a high Occult as well. It also introduced a suggestion that each rite (in general, not just for this process) cost xp equal to its level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T21:07:10-08:00","id":803563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803495#post803495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bone Flowers introduced a theoretical equivalence for some necromancy rituals, requiring Rituals at one level higher than the minimum Discipline rating of the ritual to be learned, and a high Occult as well. It also introduced a suggestion that each rite (in general, not just for this process) cost xp equal to its level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am familiar. What I was getting at is Blood magic already is &quot;Wierd powers no one else can get&quot; with a bunch of rituals on top of that. Giovanni make it worse by making you practically have to learn wraith to use Necro. It was par for the course for V:TM to have all the issues KOTE apparently brings to the table long before KOTE Showed up. Try showing Tzim stuff to slavs its.. hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T01:39:46-08:00","id":803619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803563#post803563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try showing Tzim stuff to slavs its.. hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. But I don't really mind that my fictional bodyhorror monsters have nothing to do with the actual myths, cultures and history of this part of the world. They're still intriguing characters, and I can flesh their history out better while keeping the abject terror. On that topic, I find it hillarious how people pan the concept of the Kindred of the East a horrifying amalgamation taken out of context, when the Kindred are no better. Vampires take from Stoker via Anne Rice, and neither of them have anything to do with actual myths and legends from these parts.<br /> <br /> I've found the Shadow Lords even funnier. Their nebulous &quot;Balkanness&quot; is completely taken out of context for the religion, geography and history of the area. At times it looked to me like the authors had a very poor grasp about the difference between Romania, Serbia, Hungary, Croatia, Ukraine* or Bulgaria. Or how the tribebook doesn't even dwell on the 600 years of Cold and hot war with the Turks that shaped the region (yet it spends two pages on Vlad Tepes). They couldn't even keep their mythologies straight between the Russian and the southern Slavs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T02:30:32-08:00","id":803635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803619#post803619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is. But I don't really mind that my fictional bodyhorror monsters have nothing to do with the actual myths, cultures and history of this part of the world. They're still intriguing characters, and I can flesh their history out better while keeping the abject terror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I like the Tzim the less they try to place them in some sort of mythic context. Body Horror Alien Vampires? Its coming out of left field but its a thing! Then they try to throw in Koldunism and Slavic words and its all &quot;Google Translate should not be your source of vocabulary&quot;. Really just about anything that wasn't American and to an extent even then was hilariously off centered(Wasn't there a sewers of New Orleans?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On that topic, I find it hillarious how people pan the concept of the Kindred of the East a horrifying amalgamation taken out of context, when the Kindred are no better. Vampires take from Stoker via Anne Rice, and neither of them have anything to do with actual myths and legends from these parts. </div> </div> </div>Pretty much its why I can't take the complaint that &quot;Oh they took this idea from anime&quot; seriously. Masquerade is an amalgam of random parts stolen from pop culture. Not just for vampires but most of its take on how Christianity works. But people over look it so they can play cool Vampires like out of stories. I don't see why &quot;I want to play an anime horror bad ass vampire&quot; is any less valid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've found the Shadow Lords even funnier. Their nebulous &quot;Balkanness&quot; is completely taken out of context for the religion, geography and history of the area. At times it looked to me like the authors had a very poor grasp about the difference between Romania, Serbia, Hungary, Croatia, Ukraine* or Bulgaria. Or how the tribebook doesn't even dwell on the 600 years of Cold and hot war with the Turks that shaped the region (yet it spends two pages on Vlad Tepes). They couldn't even keep their mythologies straight between the Russian and the southern Slavs. </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to say what set the tone for where Werewolf was going with ethnicities was &quot;Irish werewolves get as one of their starting power options magical drinking powers&quot;. It has gotten better but.. man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:54:53-08:00","id":803685,"title":"","content":"On amalgam of ideas. Tzimisce borrow in part from Brian Lumley's Necroscope series of books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:37:03-08:00","id":803703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803685#post803685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On amalgam of ideas. Tzimisce borrow in part from Brian Lumley's Necroscope series of books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, WoD takes from a zillion sources, it's a part of its charm, as it's a kitchensink of the highest order. It's just that the clearest influences for Kindred society is the Stoker vampire as reinterpreted through Anne Rice's lens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T13:08:54-08:00","id":803964,"title":"","content":"Being inspired by anime isn't people's major gripe with Kindred of the East. It's the Orientalism and yellow peril. I like the anime stuff too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T18:52:36-08:00","id":804189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803964#post803964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being inspired by anime isn't people's major gripe with Kindred of the East. It's the Orientalism and yellow peril. I like the anime stuff too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The criticism was usually slightly more complex than that, leveling that there was too much pop culture from Japan and not enough from Korea, Vietnam, and other places that it was ostensibly blanketing. Heresies of the Way started to get into this, but it was one of the last books in the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T19:11:02-08:00","id":804212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=804189#post804189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The criticism was usually slightly more complex than that, leveling that there was too much pop culture from Japan and not enough from Korea, Vietnam, and other places that it was ostensibly blanketing. Heresies of the Way started to get into this, but it was one of the last books in the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a problem too, although probably not the part that offended people the most. It was the Orientalism and yellow peril which did that. There's a big thing in Vampire about the invading Wan Kuei and their hatred of the West. That always seemed like the first and biggest issue to address. The narrow focus can be more easily addressed, and probably would have resolved itself after a time as more supplements came out and defined previously ignored areas of Asia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T17:37:08-08:00","id":804845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=804189#post804189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The criticism was usually slightly more complex than that, leveling that there was too much pop culture from Japan and not enough from Korea, Vietnam, and other places that it was ostensibly blanketing. Heresies of the Way started to get into this, but it was one of the last books in the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this was pretty much the biggest problem. Japan got the most coverage with China coming in a far second. The rest just didn't get enough love. Interestingly the core actually gave them a fairer shake then the rest of the line. The Companion and Heresies of the Way were probably the books that tried the most to actually start considering the gigantic swath of Earth they are supposed to cover<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=804212#post804212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a problem too, although probably not the part that offended people the most. It was the Orientalism and yellow peril which did that. There's a big thing in Vampire about the invading Wan Kuei and their hatred of the West. That always seemed like the first and biggest issue to address. The narrow focus can be more easily addressed, and probably would have resolved itself after a time as more supplements came out and defined previously ignored areas of Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orientalism came from the Asian kitchensink and the desire to shunt inside as many kung fu tropes and asian myths as they could. It's not much worse then what's done in Vampire (especialy in the first edition).. With more research and context given to the cultures and mythologies of Asia, it could have been quite more engaging. And frankly the exoticism can be a positive quality as well - one of the main reasons we play these games we do is to be different from who, what, when and how we are.<br /> <br /> The Yellow Peril is a funny case. They really have a nasty vibe of &quot;Kill Whitey&quot; And &quot;Kuei Jin are out to rule the world&quot;. But if you actually scratch below the surface (and San Francisco) you realise that came from a very misguided attmept by the authors to separate Kindred and Kuei Jin. They wanted to make them different and make it obvious they don't work together and that the Kindred are unwelcome in Asia. The core intent was to underscore how Kindred of the East was supposed to be a drastically different game from Vampire. Poor forethought combined with the fact that the authors lived through the Japanese invasion of the late 80s and the early 90s, and you suddenly have a number of books talking about Undead Fu Manchu The Revengeancing. Mind you, the line as a whole doesn't really give a fuck, it takes way more time talking about stuff it's actually about.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T17:41:08-08:00","id":804848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803703#post803703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, WoD takes from a zillion sources, it's a part of its charm, as it's a kitchensink of the highest order. It's just that the clearest influences for Kindred society is the Stoker vampire as reinterpreted through Anne Rice's lens.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I was just mentioning an influence. Relax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:29:05-08:00","id":804966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803964#post803964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being inspired by anime isn't people's major gripe with Kindred of the East. It's the Orientalism and yellow peril. I like the anime stuff too.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are alot of people who have different gripes, those might not be YOUR major gripes but plenty of people will just complain about the &quot;anime ruining my World of Darkness&quot; Also.. Every damn thing wants to kill Kindred in the CWoD, the GLO wasn't all that different from a Sabbat Seige, but no one ever puts the out the unfortunate implications of an organization in Mexico slowly taking over via violence 'proper america&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:58:23-08:00","id":805035,"title":"","content":"The GLO wasn't a single siege...<br /> <br /> And yeah, there's a big difference between Asians conspiring to use Asian communities on the west coast to infiltrate and invade the USA, and Europeans using Mexico as one of many staging grounds to duke out control over North America against another group of Europeans that are stronger in the US/Canada.<br /> <br /> One is pretty much impossible to separate from the racism of the yellow peril, while the other is a massive stretch to try to link to Mexican illegal immigration racial politics in the USA.<br /> <br /> Nobody points out the &quot;unfortunate implications&quot; of the Sabbat being in Mexico, because they don't really exist. Mexican's aren't being persecuted in the US because European based terrorist groups are directing them to attack US cities. Asians in the US were absolutely persecuted because of fear that they were avenues for the &quot;yellow horde&quot; to force their way into white America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T23:15:24-08:00","id":805044,"title":"","content":"Erm, the Sabbat of the modern era is based in Mexico City. That's where the Regent presides and everything. And if it weren't, your argument would be pretty pedantic- the core point of the Sabbat being an evil force invading out of Mexico is an inherently awkward parallel to fear and furor over illegal immigration out of Mexico and Latin America in the contemporary United States. Virtually any analogy or parallel can be dismissed by blatant overfitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T01:59:50-08:00","id":805084,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat's main base is in Mexico, yes. They're not a Mexican faction of vampires. Mexico city is just their base of operations. They have powerful and influential members from all over the globe. Their strongest and eldest members are all from Eurasia. The two Regents since the Sabbat came to the Americas were both from Europe, with the false-Regent from New York. <br /> <br /> The problem with your assertion is that the Sabbat <i>are not an invading force</i> from Mexico. They started with all of mainland North American as under their thumb until the Sabbat civil wars allowed the Camarilla to invade from Europe (which lead to the Sabbat moving their base to Mexico City later). They've controlled large swathes of modern day Canada and the USA for centuries. New Amsterdam/New York was a Sabbat city until 1999. Miami has been a Sabbat city since Europeans settled it (and is one of their major military bases for striking the Camarilla strongholds along the east coast).<br /> <br /> Saying the Sabbat is &quot;Mexicans invading,&quot; is simply inaccurate to the setting presented. The &quot;parallels&quot; don't actually exist without massively ignoring or misrepresenting the setting material.<br /> <br /> And this is still a piss-poor comparison to KotE's issues with the yellow peril issue. The yellow peril wasn't about national identity. It was about lumping all south-east Asians together as one racist caricature that Europeans needed to keep in their place. The GLO is taking an explicitly racist propoganda piece, and making it true in the WoD. It would be like having a cabal of Jewish Nephandi that mind control world leaders, and secretly have total control over the banks. It's not just a bit of stretch-to-the-point-of-ridiculous &quot;awkward parallels&quot; like, &quot;there's tensions between the US and Mexico, and the Sabbat HQ is in Mexico... so VtM is trying to say that all Mexicans crossing the borders are gang members, mules, and etc.&quot; It's actively making a racist fiction true in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T04:51:57-08:00","id":805149,"title":"","content":"I hate Vampire, both The Masquerade and The Requiem.<br /> <br /> Yet, I love Kindred of the East. It's a completely different game with completely different themes; if anything, it's closer to Wraith than to Vampire. Much of the criticism about it hinges on how the book had the characters being xenophobic against the Western vampires, which was clearly just a way to point how the Kuei-Jin were an independent entity with next to no link to the Masquerade setting, and not just a supplement to that line. It could have been done better, sure, but it was clearly necessary considering how we still have people saying that the Kuei-Kin should just be replaced by V:tM vampires in an Eastern setting.<br /> <br /> I really hope we get to see a Kindred of the East Anniversary Edition, as its own book instead of as a Vampire supplement.<br /> <br /> And, by the way, this topic was not about KotE, it was asking if other 20th Anniversary Editions will be done. I would really like a Demon: The Fallen Anniversary Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2518-erasculio","name":"Erasculio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2518_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:58:31-08:00","id":805283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805084#post805084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat's main base is in Mexico, yes. They're not a Mexican faction of vampires. Mexico city is just their base of operations. They have powerful and influential members from all over the globe. Their strongest and eldest members are all from Eurasia. The two Regents since the Sabbat came to the Americas were both from Europe, with the false-Regent from New York. <br /> <br /> The problem with your assertion is that the Sabbat <i>are not an invading force</i> from Mexico. They started with all of mainland North American as under their thumb until the Sabbat civil wars allowed the Camarilla to invade from Europe (which lead to the Sabbat moving their base to Mexico City later). They've controlled large swathes of modern day Canada and the USA for centuries. New Amsterdam/New York was a Sabbat city until 1999. Miami has been a Sabbat city since Europeans settled it (and is one of their major military bases for striking the Camarilla strongholds along the east coast).<br /> <br /> Saying the Sabbat is &amp;quot;Mexicans invading,&amp;quot; is simply inaccurate to the setting presented. The &amp;quot;parallels&amp;quot; don't actually exist without massively ignoring or misrepresenting the setting material.<br /> <br /> And this is still a piss-poor comparison to KotE's issues with the yellow peril issue. The yellow peril wasn't about national identity. It was about lumping all south-east Asians together as one racist caricature that Europeans needed to keep in their place. The GLO is taking an explicitly racist propoganda piece, and making it true in the WoD. It would be like having a cabal of Jewish Nephandi that mind control world leaders, and secretly have total control over the banks. It's not just a bit of stretch-to-the-point-of-ridiculous &amp;quot;awkward parallels&amp;quot; like, &amp;quot;there's tensions between the US and Mexico, and the Sabbat HQ is in Mexico... so VtM is trying to say that all Mexicans crossing the borders are gang members, mules, and etc.&amp;quot; It's actively making a racist fiction true in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this. Focusing too much on Japan is an issue, but it's not so much an offensive issue. Racist caricatures are. So out of the two issues, the latter is a bigger problem for me. As always, YMMV, but it's the racist caricatures that David A. Hill seemed to mention the most when he explained why he didn't think OPP would do a KotE 20, and not so much the narrow focus (although he did discuss that too). Hence why I said I think it's the primary issue preventing us from getting an anniversary edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T09:24:37-08:00","id":805290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805283#post805283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that David A. Hill seemed to mention the most when he explained why he didn't think OPP would do a KotE 20, and not so much the narrow focus (although he did discuss that too). Hence why I said I think it's the primary issue preventing us from getting an anniversary edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone has the same opinion that David Hill(or you) has. And last I checked, David Hill has not supplanted Rich Thomas as head of Onyx Path. One person, living in Japan for a few years, does not speak for the entire world. <br /> <br /> If Onyx Path feels the fans want it(we do), and if Onyx Path feels it will sell(it would), and if the new White Wolf Publishing is in favor of it(they would be, IMO), then it will be done. <br /> <br /> And if the subject matter is handled with respect, and some things are updated, and you still hate it will all your might? You still have the option of not buying it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T09:33:12-08:00","id":805298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805290#post805290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not everyone has the same opinion that David Hill(or you) has. And last I checked, David Hill has not supplanted Rich Thomas as head of Onyx Path. One person, living in Japan for a few years, does not speak for the entire world. <br /> <br /> If Onyx Path feels the fans want it(we do), and if Onyx Path feels it will sell(it would), and if the new White Wolf Publishing is in favor of it(they would be, IMO), then it will be done. <br /> <br /> And if the subject matter is handled with respect, and some things are updated, and you still hate it will all your might? You still have the option of not buying it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm asking for the subject to be handled with respect, so I don't see the need for your snide tone, to be honest.<br /> <br /> Plus, I never said I hated the game. I've played it and liked it. But looking back at it now, I see lots of stuff that's just problematic and racist. Hence why I'm saying that stuff should be fixed if they do another version, not that it shouldn't be made. But I also feel, given the way M20 was written and the changes implemented in V20DA, RichT would probably be aware of the issues with racism in the book and would probably be aware that that adds an extra level of difficulty with reviving the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T14:26:21-08:00","id":805491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat's main base is in Mexico, yes. They're not a Mexican faction of vampires. Mexico city is just their base of operations. They have powerful and influential members from all over the globe. Their strongest and eldest members are all from Eurasia. The two Regents since the Sabbat came to the Americas were both from Europe, with the false-Regent from New York. </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I talked about with regards to overfitting. The (oftentimes incredibly silly) history of the World of Darkness that explains how we got to this point is irrelevant- what matters on the first, gut appraisal is the ground-level situation as of the actual timepoint of Masquerade. That is to say, with the unwashed raping hordes of savages pouring forth out of Mexico and Central America and increasingly overrunning the USA, with contributions from uhhh....black and poor Detroit (Montreal is the obvious exception here, but I assumed that was mostly a deliberate jab at the rudeness of the stereotypical Quebecois). The supplements even note how the Sabbat is comprised in much larger part than the Camarilla of black and latin american types. If you're going to insist that this isn't a parallel then a bunch of East Asians in San Francisco posing a threat to the aims of a secret society lead by a cabal in Milan and a band of crazy jihadis operating out of Latin America also really can't be argued to be problematic, either.<br /> <br /> I mean, I honestly don't care either way. I consider neither the Sabbat nor the KotE to be especially 'problematic' in some sort of nonsensical political correctness sense. Both are problematic narratively- the Sabbat makes it way too easy to shove away any sense of personal horror or Elder oppression or careful intrigue because they present an immediate, unambiguous existential threat whenever they show up (I mean yes you can weave in the other elements here especially with Elders using childer as cannon fodder, etc., but still), and the KotE are another part of the setting's awful tendency to lock away huge swathes of the world from normal play. The Setites and Assamites clamp down the Middle East, we have a whole mess of different-for-the-sake-of-being different nonsense in Africa (although that's still at least nominally accessible to a variety of clans), and then the magical arbitrary Kue Jin just taking most of populated Asia out of consideration. I mean obviously you can still set Cainite stories there- but that takes out both any sense of Sect and most of the usual principals of Vampire while amping up the precariousness to often untenable degrees. Taking mesopotamia as the arbitrary starting point as per Caine myth (regardless of the accuracy of the details) and simulating the diffusion and dynamics of cainite populations across the world without arbitrary recourse to 'ethnic clans' or magical special different mysterious East would've been far preferable to what we got in OWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 01-10-2016, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T14:40:39-08:00","id":805501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erasculio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805149#post805149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, by the way, this topic was not about KotE, it was asking if other 20th Anniversary Editions will be done. I would really like a Demon: The Fallen Anniversary Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately it is pretty unavoidable. While people have their personal tastes on Hunter, Demon, and Mummy, KotE is the contentious one of the bunch. It is unfortunately part of the calculus for all of these. If one of the group doesn't get an update, it's going to be a PR problem, even if there's no huge fan division with the rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805290#post805290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everyone has the same opinion that David Hill(or you) has. And last I checked, David Hill has not supplanted Rich Thomas as head of Onyx Path. One person, living in Japan for a few years, does not speak for the entire world.<br /> <br /> If Onyx Path feels the fans want it(we do), and if Onyx Path feels it will sell(it would), and if the new White Wolf Publishing is in favor of it(they would be, IMO), then it will be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of hypocritical to throw out, &quot;you don't speak for everyone,&quot; to the people that disagree with you, while then immediately claiming to speak for everyone.<br /> <br /> Not all the fans want it. Not every fan is convinced it <i>should</i> sell whether it would or not. It's a divisive issue. You don't have any place to talk about what Onyx Path, or the fans as a whole, think.<br /> <br /> It's also getting a bit ridiculous to continually skip that David Hill has been one of the go-to Onyx Path freelancers for helping making sure that problematic WoD material is treated with more respect as it gets updated for the X20 era books. One of the people that has had a huge impact on Onyx Path avoiding many of the failures to do things respectfully in the past, which has let the company gain a superior reputation for being capable of doing so, is one of the people that doesn't feel KotE can adequately get a 20th book and fix it to those standards; it can be one, or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:02:33-08:00","id":805516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805491#post805491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what matters on the first, gut appraisal is the ground-level situation as of the actual timepoint of Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. Then the parallels of the Sabbat to the US immigration racial politics still makes no sense. The ground-level situation of the actual timepoint of 1991-to now in the setting is that the Sabbat controls almost all of North America save the north east coast and some of the great lakes (Cam territory) and the west coast (Anarch territory).<br /> <br /> You can't paint them as invaders. They're trying to reclaim territory others took from them. They're not, according to the text, &quot;pouring forth out of Mexico and Central America,&quot; they're already in the USA and Canada, and have been for as long as is relevant. Their attack forces are based on locals resources, not hordes coming from outside.<br /> <br /> Unless you're going to try to use, &quot;gut appraisal,&quot; to mean, &quot;whatever I want to claim because it doesn't have to do with whats in the books with an semblance of accuracy,&quot; the ground-level situation doesn't parallel what you're saying it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I consider neither the Sabbat nor the KotE to be especially 'problematic' in some sort of nonsensical political correctness sense. </div> </div> </div>Why did you have to go there? You're basically saying that the racism in books like KotE or WOD: Gypsies, doesn't matter because political correctness is a vague word that makes things not matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:44:06-08:00","id":805551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erasculio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805149#post805149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much of the criticism about it hinges on how the book had the characters being xenophobic against the Western vampires, which was clearly just a way to point how the Kuei-Jin were an independent entity with next to no link to the Masquerade setting, and not just a supplement to that line. It could have been done better, sure, but it was clearly necessary considering how we still have people saying that the Kuei-Kin should just be replaced by V:tM vampires in an Eastern setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the writers wanted to point out how the Kuei-jin were an independent entity with next to no link to the Masquerade setting, they could have accomplished that more easily by not calling the book <i>Kindred of the East</i> and printing the words &quot;A sourcebook for Vampire: The Masquerade&quot; on the cover.<br /> <br /> People want Western-style Kindred in an Eastern setting because they want to use <i>one</i> set of rules at a time. The Laibon may suffer from a &quot;Western clans in funny hats&quot; syndrome, but at least you can mix Kindred and Laibon together relatively painlessly in chronicles that span the globe. Not so with the Kuei-jin: unlike every other supernatural faction in the World of Darkness, Kuei-jin essentially lock Kindred out of an entire <i>continent,</i> whereas the Kuei-jin themselves have no such restrictions. Imagine if North America was werewolf country where the Garou instantly ripped off the heads of any mages that tried to place a foot on US soil, and not only did American players have no inspirational material for playing mages in the US, but the suggestion that there should be official support for US mages was actively frowned upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:51:30-08:00","id":805555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=803964#post803964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being inspired by anime isn't people's major gripe with Kindred of the East. It's the Orientalism and yellow peril. I like the anime stuff too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This<br /> <br /> I agree with this statement in its entirety. And I am a huge anime fan whose World of Darkness games tend to hew towards anime action-adventure. But Kindred of the East was just awful in my book.<br /> <br /> Which is why in my games, Cainite vampires rule East Asia's cities, though due to stark cultural differences between Asian and European vampires, the Camarilla and Sabbat have little to no sway in Asia. The Kindred there prefer the rule of the local vampire courts that have been in place for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> But enough about KOTE, the issue at hand is further X20 game lines. I think C20 will probably be the last. Given the divisive nature of how Wraith and Changeling originally were, I'm legitimately surprised we got 20th Anniversary Editions after M20. But I can see Wr20 and C20 getting released due to the nostalgia value alone and because despite the problems in both gamelines, there were a lot of good ideas that were cut short.<br /> <br /> As for KOTE, Hunter, and Demon, they don't have near the amount of fanbase the original five gamelines have.<br /> <br /> Demon is way too recent of a gameline to have any real nostalgia value attached to it and the whole Earthbound stuff has a lot of potentially offensive material regarding religion (The whole &quot;All religions except Christianity were created by the Earthbound and therefore false and evil!&quot; It's a pretty rotten thing to say when you read it out loud). That being said, if Demon were to get an X20-style anniversary treatment, the whole Earthbound debacle could easily be cleaned up and fixed.<br /> <br /> KOTE is a very problematic and controversial gameline that probably won't get an X20 release due to its issues (though I could see a Kuei-Jin supplement book for V20 or Wraith 20), and Hunter: The Reckoning is probably the least popular of the Classic World of Darkness gamelines (unless you count Mummy as a full gameline), so I doubt we'll see X20 books for these gamelines.<br /> <br /> Then again, I thought we'd never see X20 books for Wraith or Changeling, and yet they're both in development. So I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T16:30:14-08:00","id":805579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805035#post805035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The GLO wasn't a single siege...<br /> <br /> And yeah, there's a big difference between Asians conspiring to use Asian communities on the west coast to infiltrate and invade the USA, and Europeans using Mexico as one of many staging grounds to duke out control over North America against another group of Europeans that are stronger in the US/Canada.<br /> <br /> One is pretty much impossible to separate from the racism of the yellow peril, while the other is a massive stretch to try to link to Mexican illegal immigration racial politics in the USA.<br /> <br /> Nobody points out the &quot;unfortunate implications&quot; of the Sabbat being in Mexico, because they don't really exist. Mexican's aren't being persecuted in the US because European based terrorist groups are directing them to attack US cities. Asians in the US were absolutely persecuted because of fear that they were avenues for the &quot;yellow horde&quot; to force their way into white America.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IT has nothing to do with illegal immigration policies in the United States but IT DOES look alot like some of the kookier Extreme Right Wing/Evangelical views on things. Just like alot of the portrayals of Catholicism look driven by a combination of Pop culture and anticatholic stereotypes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T16:36:16-08:00","id":805587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805551#post805551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the writers wanted to point out how the Kuei-jin were an independent entity with next to no link to the Masquerade setting, they could have accomplished that more easily by not calling the book <i>Kindred of the East</i> and printing the words &quot;A sourcebook for Vampire: The Masquerade&quot; on the cover.<br /> <br /> People want Western-style Kindred in an Eastern setting because they want to use <i>one</i> set of rules at a time. The Laibon may suffer from a &quot;Western clans in funny hats&quot; syndrome, but at least you can mix Kindred and Laibon together relatively painlessly in chronicles that span the globe. Not so with the Kuei-jin: unlike every other supernatural faction in the World of Darkness, Kuei-jin essentially lock Kindred out of an entire <i>continent,</i> whereas the Kuei-jin themselves have no such restrictions. Imagine if North America was werewolf country where the Garou instantly ripped off the heads of any mages that tried to place a foot on US soil, and not only did American players have no inspirational material for playing mages in the US, but the suggestion that there should be official support for US mages was actively frowned upon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Except actually you can't. Laibon lose their nature if they leave africa and there are kindred who have been there centuries who haven't picked up Aya and Orun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:03:01-08:00","id":805613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805587#post805587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except actually you can't. Laibon lose their nature if they leave africa and there are kindred who have been there centuries who haven't picked up Aya and Orun</div> </div> </div> </div>What? The mechanical differences between Kindred and Laibon can be counted with one hand, while Kindred and Kuei-jin share practically no mechanics beyond the basic attributes and abilities shared by all WoD splats.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I guess &quot;mixing together&quot; Kindred and Laibon was phrased unclearly. I simply mean that it's easy to run a chronicle with both Kindred and Laibon characters, because the mechanical differences are minor issues, compared to how separate from each other VtM and KotE are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 01-10-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:00:17-08:00","id":805650,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, where do people see a huge anime influence in <b>Kindred of the East</b>? I've got the corebook, the five Dharma books, and <b>Shadow War</b> . . . and I'm not seeing much anime, or even Japanese, influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T19:22:42-08:00","id":805705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805650#post805650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, where do people see a huge anime influence in <b>Kindred of the East</b>? I've got the corebook, the five Dharma books, and <b>Shadow War</b> . . . and I'm not seeing much anime, or even Japanese, influence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its the Art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:19:56-08:00","id":805733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805551#post805551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the writers wanted to point out how the Kuei-jin were an independent entity with next to no link to the Masquerade setting, they could have accomplished that more easily by not calling the book <i>Kindred of the East</i> and printing the words &quot;A sourcebook for Vampire: The Masquerade&quot; on the cover.<br /> <br /> People want Western-style Kindred in an Eastern setting because they want to use <i>one</i> set of rules at a time. The Laibon may suffer from a &quot;Western clans in funny hats&quot; syndrome, but at least you can mix Kindred and Laibon together relatively painlessly in chronicles that span the globe. Not so with the Kuei-jin: unlike every other supernatural faction in the World of Darkness, Kuei-jin essentially lock Kindred out of an entire <i>continent,</i> whereas the Kuei-jin themselves have no such restrictions. Imagine if North America was werewolf country where the Garou instantly ripped off the heads of any mages that tried to place a foot on US soil, and not only did American players have no inspirational material for playing mages in the US, but the suggestion that there should be official support for US mages was actively frowned upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not terribly true. Kuei-jin have generally not succeeded well at exporting themselves in any significant numbers. The GLO, which wasn't even supported by all of them anyway, didn't even succeed. Combined with the enclaves of interaction from both sides at border regions. Just like people used to mechanically overstate the differences of Kindred and Kuei-jin, they overstate the territorial issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:24:27-08:00","id":805738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805516#post805516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you have to go there? You're basically saying that the racism in books like KotE or WOD: Gypsies, doesn't matter because political correctness is a vague word that makes things not matter</div> </div> </div> </div>Because not everyone(was that okay?) sees the racism and/or the same issues that you do. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:31:55-08:00","id":805743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805555#post805555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and <b>Hunter: The Reckoning is probably the least popular </b>of the Classic World of Darkness gamelines (unless you count Mummy as a full gameline), so I doubt we'll see X20 books for these gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Link? Because I guarantee you're wrong. <br /> <br /> I'll wait for you to scrounge up your sources. <br /> <br /> Because from what devs has said, Hunter was pretty damn successful--especially compared to Wraith, Demon, Changeling, and Mummy. Hell, it also received THREE popular videogames for Xbox and Playstation 2. <br /> <br /> These threads always turn out the same. People crapping all over other people's favorites because of their own personal preferences, and then other people getting offended(like myself) when people decide to bring their own personal ideologies and/or societal issues into a discussion about why X can or will not work. <br /> <br /> I'm not perfect, however. And realize my thin skin only gets me into trouble when this kind of talk begins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:35:59-08:00","id":805745,"title":"","content":"For posterity, no Mummy wasn't a full line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:37:34-08:00","id":805746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805743#post805743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Link? Because I guarantee you're wrong.<br /> <br /> I'll wait for you to scrounge up your sources.<br /> <br /> Because from what devs has said, Hunter was pretty damn successful--especially compared to Wraith, Demon, Changeling, and Mummy. Hell, it also received THREE popular videogames for Xbox and Playstation 2.<br /> <br /> These threads always turn out the same. People crapping all over other people's favorites because of their own personal preferences, and then other people getting offended(like myself) when people decide to bring their own personal ideologies and/or societal issues into a discussion about why X can or will not work.<br /> <br /> I'm not perfect, however. And realize my thin skin only gets me into trouble when this kind of talk begins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, maybe I was wrong on a certain level. From what I hear, Hunter was very successful financially (it sold well, but not as well as Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage) but flopped critically with the fanbase. Everyone I know on the old forum bashed Reckoning constantly.<br /> <br /> That being said, the fanbase also loves Wraith which sold the worst of all the gamelines (hence its early cancellation), so who knows?<br /> <br /> I mean, I like Reckoning, but I always thought I was in the minority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:47:43-08:00","id":805757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805746#post805746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>but flopped critically with the fanbase</b>. Everyone I know on the old forum bashed Reckoning constantly.<br /> <br /> I mean, I like Reckoning, but I always thought I was in the minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, we're all speaking for everyone now. lol. <br /> <br /> I LOVE Reckoning. Love it. And I know a number of people that do, too. Reckoning was/is a fantastic game. Matter of fact, its my favorite WoD game. So it didn't flop critically with everyone. Some liked it, some did not. Just like Vampire, Wraith, Changeling, Mage, etc. <br /> <br /> Don't underestimate the strength of HtR as a gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:58:31-08:00","id":805764,"title":"","content":"Without numbers from former employees,etc it's somewhat hard to tell because forum presence tends to not be a good indicator of popularity to a certain extent. I know the stuff about the dichotomy of the mechanics and the art was mentioned a lot with Hunter. I generally liked the game and enjoyed using them in end of the world campaigns, particularly with Demon. I never got to play many games of it. I like Vigil more but nothing about Reckonings set up bothered me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:15:30-08:00","id":805805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805738#post805738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because not everyone(was that okay?) sees the racism and/or the same issues that you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not seeing things the same way as I do is fine. Throwing out, &quot;political correctness,&quot; as a shield from actually having to back up what you see in the books however, is not (from either side really, there's a reason people haven't just said, &quot;KotE is racist!&quot; but actually detailed what's problematic about it from a racism angle).<br /> <br /> That's the problem with this whole aspect of the criticisms of KotE on grounds of racism issues. The games vocal defenders of its status quo either say, &quot;it can all be fixed even if I have zero solutions, that's not my job,&quot; or, &quot;it's not really racist, you're just being PC, so I don't acknowledge anything should change.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's why these threads endlessly recycle the same bullshit conversations There's no actual desire to discuss things in a fashion that could actually move anything forward. No solutions proffered the would change the problems with the game while keeping it true to its roots that can be collectively hashed out. Which leaves the people that think it needs to be changed fairly dramatically being told, &quot;that's too much for it to be a KotE20 book,&quot; and the people that don't think it needs major change defending it warts and all instead of looking at what can be changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T00:10:52-08:00","id":805856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805746#post805746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, maybe I was wrong on a certain level. From what I hear, Hunter was very successful financially (it sold well, but not as well as Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage) but flopped critically with the fanbase. Everyone I know on the old forum bashed Reckoning constantly.<br /> <br /> That being said, the fanbase also loves Wraith which sold the worst of all the gamelines (hence its early cancellation), so who knows?<br /> <br /> I mean, I like Reckoning, but I always thought I was in the minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't base forum dislike with fanbase dislike. It's an easy mistake to make, but an incorrect one. If it were true, VtM would also be a flop with the fanbase, because there are hundreds of threads flaming this or that aspect of the game. Reckoning clearly had the sales to support it, which strongly suggests the fanbase didn't turn away from it or hate it or what have you. Because if they did, the obvious question becomes &quot;who kept buying the products?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T02:04:31-08:00","id":805912,"title":"","content":"I'd wager that HtR had a mixed blessing in being very popular for a WoD game outside of the core WoD fanbase; hence having a fairly poor reputation among hardcore WoD fans (I can attest to this not being a solely forum based thing, I've run into the attitude plenty at conventions and such back when it came out). HtR has a lot of appeal for people that might like the general idea of the WoD, but don't want to deal with the things that most WoD fans consider major elements of the games. You don't have to worry about learning tons of backstory and metaplot. You don't have to buy books from other games with new systems to get more than 2-3 pages on major supernatural entities. You don't have to play a monster struggling with their nature (whether a vampire struggling to remain human, a werewolf struggling to not rage-out and murder everyone they care about, a mage struggling to avoid hubris and power to strive for enlightenment, etc.). And it is a game where you can (try to) play an unambiguous good guy; which is not to say that grey and grey morality of most of the WoD is bad or that HtR lacks moral complexity, just that you can run it easily without the PCs invested in being morally compromised from the get go.<br /> <br /> Anecdotal as it is, I'd say more people that are big fans of HtR aren't fans of the WoD in general (not that they actively dislike the rest of the games or anything, there's a difference between fan and people that will play if that's what the group is playing), than people that are big fans of HtR and the WoD in general. At conventions with fairly regular WoD fans (one of which was run by a LARP group and used their yearly convention as a big event for their on-going Vampire LARP), I would say around 80% of people playing in one-shots I ran for any other game line were WoD regulars, and 10% were people they were looking to get introduced to the games, with the remainder being straggler curious types. Doing HtR one-shots was a crap shoot if I'd even have players, and when I did it was very reversed with around 80% being the curious stragglers, and a good portion of the rest being HtR fans of mixed fandom towards the other WoD games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:12:51-08:00","id":805940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805912#post805912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;some good observations&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually makes a lot of sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:30:40-08:00","id":805950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805650#post805650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, where do people see a huge anime influence in <b>Kindred of the East</b>? I've got the corebook, the five Dharma books, and <b>Shadow War</b> . . . and I'm not seeing much anime, or even Japanese, influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Disciplines mostly. Which shouldn't be a problem. The art is distinctly not Anime (unless it's people hating on Mel's specific style, but I have little nice to say about those people). Exalted was the one with anime art.<br /> <br /> A lot of the terminology and mythological cues are taken from Japan and japanese mthology, and the Chinese sources while interesting, are not researched all that well. I know that Dino has a pet peeve with Tou Mu as a Yama King stemming from D&amp;Disms. Also, China is presented as one people and one culture, and they're quite a bit more complex than that. Southeast Asia, Korea, Mongolia, Tibet and India get barely any coverage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:01:05-08:00","id":806044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805805#post805805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why these threads endlessly recycle the same bullshit conversations There's no actual desire to discuss things in a fashion that could actually move anything forward. No solutions proffered the would change the problems with the game while keeping it true to its roots that can be collectively hashed out. Which leaves the people that think it needs to be changed fairly dramatically being told, &quot;that's too much for it to be a KotE20 book,&quot; and the people that don't think it needs major change defending it warts and all instead of looking at what can be changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> <br /> Who knows what the future will bring, but I'm positive if WWP gives OP the go ahead to do a new version of KotE, they will handle it with the same respect as they have the rest of their releases(both CWoD and CroD).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:04:16-08:00","id":806045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805856#post805856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Don't base forum dislike with fanbase dislike.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't have said it any better. For example, I haven't run into many people on these forums that are big fans of Malkavians. When I look around other places on the internet(Facebook, for example)? There are literally thousands of people who find that clan their favorite. People wearing Malkavian shirts, buying the books, etc. etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:12:42-08:00","id":806505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=805950#post805950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Disciplines mostly. Which shouldn't be a problem. The art is distinctly not Anime (unless it's people hating on Mel's specific style, but I have little nice to say about those people). Exalted was the one with anime art.<br /> <br /> A lot of the terminology and mythological cues are taken from Japan and japanese mthology, and the Chinese sources while interesting, are not researched all that well. I know that Dino has a pet peeve with Tou Mu as a Yama King stemming from D&amp;Disms. Also, China is presented as one people and one culture, and they're quite a bit more complex than that. Southeast Asia, Korea, Mongolia, Tibet and India get barely any coverage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kind of want to know why this standard is NEVER held for Masquerade. Its Shit biblical, historical and the mythology is all less than 2 centuries old as a base. Masquerade Set has more on common with RE Howard's Conan than anything you'd get from some research into Egyptian myth. Yet its just accepted. Meanwhile Vampire as someone who died and comes back is.. a fairly universal concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:39:21-08:00","id":806527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=806505#post806505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I kind of want to know why this standard is NEVER held for Masquerade. Its Shit biblical, historical and the mythology is all less than 2 centuries old as a base. Masquerade Set has more on common with RE Howard's Conan than anything you'd get from some research into Egyptian myth. Yet its just accepted. Meanwhile Vampire as someone who died and comes back is.. a fairly universal concept.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is my primary irritation and I'm glad you articulated it. It's rather jarring to see someone in the same breathe bat not an eye for one sort of poor myth making and taking then blast another. There are rooms for improvement across the board and I cannot help but feel like picking out KotE as some sort of special creature in regards to that is both odd and itself a sort of concern trolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 01-11-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:10:21-08:00","id":806585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=806505#post806505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I kind of want to know why this standard is NEVER held for Masquerade. Its Shit biblical, historical and the mythology is all less than 2 centuries old as a base. Masquerade Set has more on common with RE Howard's Conan than anything you'd get from some research into Egyptian myth. Yet its just accepted. Meanwhile Vampire as someone who died and comes back is.. a fairly universal concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I want to give both the present Set and Tou Mu the boot. I even made a suggestion during W20 open development to eject anything having to do directly with V:tM from the history of the Silent Striders so they could be not connected to REH Set vampires, but that obviously didn't happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:25:46-08:00","id":806595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=806505#post806505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of want to know why this standard is NEVER held for Masquerade. Its Shit biblical, historical and the mythology is all less than 2 centuries old as a base. Masquerade Set has more on common with RE Howard's Conan than anything you'd get from some research into Egyptian myth. Yet its just accepted.</div> </div> </div> </div>These things are brought up <i>all the time,</i> though. I can't even recall the last time there was a topic about Set on the Vampire subforum where somebody <i>didn't</i> mention what a mythological shitshow the Setites are. These complaints are in no way limited to <i>Kindred of the East,</i> unless you expect people to also list criticisms about unrelated topics <i>in the same post</i> where they criticize KotE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile Vampire as someone who died and comes back is.. a fairly universal concept. </div> </div> </div>Which is why I would love to see more support for playing such characters outside of some vaguely defined pan-Asian cultural sphere -- as well as more support for Kindred-style vampires in Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:55:22-08:00","id":806620,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Risen already exists, and Kue Jin are effectively in a metaphysical sense auto-Risen who inexplicably only arise from peoples of a specific cultural/ethnic background.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:58:52-08:00","id":806623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=806595#post806595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These complaints are in no way limited to <i>Kindred of the East,</i> unless you expect people to also list criticisms about unrelated topics <i>in the same post</i> where they criticize KotE.</div> </div> </div> </div>So very much this.<br /> <br /> The problematic elements of the WoD regardless of individual game-lines gets hashed out regularly.<br /> <br /> This thread isn't about main VtM, and all the problems with the Setites, or the Assamites, or the Ravnos, or the etc., etc., etc.<br /> <br /> I also think there is a fair allocation of energy between things that are horribly off but dealing with religions/groups that haven't existed for thousands of years, and things that are horribly off while playing into issues that living people today are dealing with. The Setites are nonsensical, but besides bothering mythology enthusiasts, the Clan isn't perpetuating harmful stereotypes like the Assamites and Ravnos are guilty of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:06:55-08:00","id":806628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=806623#post806623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So very much this.<br /> <br /> The problematic elements of the WoD regardless of individual game-lines gets hashed out regularly.<br /> <br /> This thread isn't about main VtM, and all the problems with the Setites, or the Assamites, or the Ravnos, or the etc., etc., etc.<br /> <br /> I also think there is a fair allocation of energy between things that are horribly off but dealing with religions/groups that haven't existed for thousands of years, and things that are horribly off while playing into issues that living people today are dealing with. The Setites are nonsensical, but besides bothering mythology enthusiasts, the Clan isn't perpetuating harmful stereotypes like the Assamites and Ravnos are guilty of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the depiction of the Setites outside of their personal mythology involves a rather nasty stereotypes related to racial and economic stereotypes....I am not buying this at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T22:41:24-08:00","id":806787,"title":"","content":"I'm not quite sure which you're referring too. While the Setites play into the Western/White racial trope of, &quot;other people want to steal our women,&quot; that's not a specifically Arab, Egyptian, or Muslim, racial or ethnic stereotype. It's also fairly distinctly different from how Western stereotyping of those groups go. Arabs stereotypes, especially as related to economics, are either the sleazy merchant, or the harem owning aristocrat/oil-sheik. Both of these are too overt for the Setite's as presented. The European based stereotypes were not of hidden corruption spreading cults of debauchery. The stereotypes in question are actually closer to the Ravnos: unscrupulous thieves out to screw you over in business dealing, and/or steal away your valuables before disappearing back to somewhere else (though often women are treated more as objects/valuables in these stereotypes). The Assamites cover the other major European stereotypes of Arabs, and Muslims: desert bandits and murders, or violent religious terrorists.<br /> <br /> Basically... the Setites are a stereotype that doesn't have to do with distinct real world people they're associated with. &quot;Vice pushing debauchery to tear down 'proper' social norms,&quot; isn't something Arabs, Muslims, etc. get persecuted for. The most recent form of anti-non-Jewish-Middle-Eastern stereotypes is pretty much about the exact opposite: fear that they're coming to the West to force their oppressive social norms via strict religious laws.<br /> <br /> The Setites do play into nasty modern stereotypes, but again, they're not specific to the Setites or the ethnic groups/religions associated with them, they're the standard first line European othering that applies to everyone that's not considered White and/or appropriately Christian enough. My point is not that there aren't problems with the Setites, but that the stereotypes they use are either too old to matter to living people, or too disconnected from the Setites to matter specifically to that one Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-12-2016, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T23:40:52-08:00","id":806806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/801714-okay-20th-anniversary-editions-for-the-original-five-any-more-coming?p=806505#post806505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I kind of want to know why this standard is NEVER held for Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bActually, in addition to what others have thrown in about the Settites, there have also been some loud complaints about Clan <sup>John </sup>Giovanni and Tribes <sup>Drunken Irish Hooligan</sup> Fianna and <sup>Pot Smoking Hippie Sexiness </sup>Children of Gaia. Some groups in the WoD had started to grow up, others need to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}